WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.589
Use mission and asset identifiers in file names and folders.

00:00:04.589 --> 00:00:08.630
Organize originals, working products, annotations, maps, defect records, reports,

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:09.977
and exports separately.

00:00:09.977 --> 00:00:14.915
Preserve the relationship between every reported observation and its source file.

00:00:14.915 --> 00:00:19.854
Metadata may include time, position, aircraft, sensor, camera settings, altitude estimate,

00:00:19.854 --> 00:00:21.201
and processing history.

00:00:21.201 --> 00:00:22.996
Preserve it where appropriate,

00:00:22.996 --> 00:00:28.384
but validate location after navigation anomalies and avoid treating metadata as infallible.

00:00:28.384 --> 00:00:32.424
Inspection notes should describe asset component, observation, evidence reference,

00:00:32.424 --> 00:00:35.118
environmental context, confidence, and recommended follow-up.

00:00:35.118 --> 00:00:42.301
Defect tags organize review but should not imply engineering severity unless a qualified authority assigns it.

00:00:42.301 --> 00:00:48.587
G I S integration can connect observations with approved asset layers and repeat inspections.

00:00:48.587 --> 00:00:52.627
Check coordinate reference, accuracy, asset identifiers, and map currency.

00:00:52.627 --> 00:00:57.566
A precise symbol can still be attached to uncertain source data.

00:00:57.566 --> 00:01:01.157
Reports distinguish direct observation, automated detection, analyst judgment,

00:01:01.157 --> 00:01:02.504
and specialist conclusion.

00:01:02.504 --> 00:01:06.994
Include overview and close-up evidence, limitations, missing coverage, collection conditions,

00:01:06.994 --> 00:01:09.687
and what additional inspection is needed.

00:01:09.687 --> 00:01:13.728
Infrastructure data can reveal layout, condition, access routes, vulnerabilities,

00:01:13.728 --> 00:01:15.075
and operational details.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:20.013
Apply access control, encryption and secure transfer where appropriate, backup, retention,

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:23.156
controlled sharing, and review before public release.

00:01:23.156 --> 00:01:25.400
Version reports and correction records.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:30.788
If a component label, location, interpretation, or severity changes after specialist review,

00:01:30.788 --> 00:01:36.175
preserve the superseded conclusion and explain the update so downstream teams do

00:01:36.175 --> 00:01:38.420
not act on stale findings.
